  "body": "The public directory crashed when an optional city preference could not be read or saved. It also allowed stale favorite controls/responses to act after a session change, including A\u2192B\u2192A. Guard preference access while preserving the search URL/input, bind favorite reads/mutations and first-value callbacks to the current session occurrence, and offer an authoritative refresh after an ambiguous failure.\n\nValidation: six original component counterexamples reproduced; 18 focused tests pass, including late private reads and failure recovery. Fifteen production-bundle browser cases pass across three engines/five profiles with denied storage, keyboard search, reload and axe. TypeScript, lint, build (365639 gzip initial JS) and strict catalog audit pass. TLC checks 208 distinct states and the dispatch/receipt mutants fail their named invariants; the full pinned TLC/Alloy suite passes.\n\nTracks UX-260917-007 and UX-260917-046 in the existing audit register and `directory-entry.md`. Browser APIs are synthetic; this does not assert new server persistence, physical assistive-technology coverage or production rollout. No migration/API/mobile contract change. Independent review, CI and deployment verification remain required.\n",
